:: Widgets Hospital [widget]
<<widget "harper_intro">><<nobr>>
<<if $hospitalintro is 0>>
	<<set $hospitalintro to 1>>

	<<npc Harper>><<person1>>You don't have to wait long. A <<if $pronoun is "m">>man<<else>>woman<</if>> wearing a white medical coat and carrying a clipboard emerges from an adjacent room and beckons you over.
	<br><br>

	<<He>> smiles at you. "Hello, I'm Doctor Harper." You enter <<his>> office and take a seat. <<He>> looks young, can't be older than 25.
	<br><br>

<<elseif $hospitalintro is "livestock">>
	<<set $hospitalintro to 1>>
	<<npc Harper>><<person1>>
	You don't have to wait long. A <<if $pronoun is "m">>man<<else>>woman<</if>> wearing a white medical coat and carrying a clipboard emerges from an adjacent room and beckons you over.
	<br><br>

	It's the doctor from the farm. The one who experimented on you. "Hello, I'm Doctor Harper." There's no recognition on <<his>> face. You hesitate, but enter <<his>> office and take a seat. You're in a busy hospital now, not an isolated farm.
	<br><br>

<<else>>

	<<npc Harper>><<person1>>You don't have to wait long. Doctor Harper emerges from <<his>> office and beckons you over. You follow <<him>> in and take a seat.
	<br><br>

<</if>>
<</nobr>><</widget>>



<<widget "harper_checkup">><<nobr>>
	<!--
	<<if $visitcount is undefined>>
		<<set $visitcount to 0>>
	<<else>>
		<<set $visitcount++>>
	<</if>>
	<<set $harpervisitstats[$visitcount] to $logged>> 
	-->
	<!--there shouldn't be need to care about stats before the last visit, in theory one could do something nice with them but doesn't seem worthwhile.-->
	
	<<set $newstats to $logged>>
	<!-- While this should work fine it'd be in some ways better if we instead went through the log entries and figured out the stats that way without needing to have another copy of the stats saved constantly but that's harder to do and if it's been a long time since last appointment events might have been cleaned up(shouldn't be too much of an issue unless we look for specific events) -->
	<!-- When this is more done could save only the variables that matter-->
	"What have you been up to?" <!--Comparing stats to ones at last appointment -->
	With a hazy and relaxed mind various things come to mind but you aren't sure which one to bring up.
		<!-- Not sure how to handle more boring and repetitive options, perhaps bringing up something you've already talked about will make Harper ask again. -->
		
		Worked in the cafe
		Danced
		Fucked animals
		Stole stuff
		Lost my _ virginity
		<<if $harpervisitstats.rapestat lte $newstats.rapestat>>
		Raped
		<</if>>
		Prostitution
<</nobr>><</widget>>

<<widget "harper_checkup_end">><<nobr>>
	<<set $harpervisitstats to $newstats>>
	<<unset $newstats>>
<</nobr>><</widget>>